# env
# Ignore every .env variant, then re-admit the committed template. The wildcard matters:
# `.env` and `.env.local` alone leave `.env.bak`, `.env.save`, `.env.prod` and whatever an
# editor or a careless backup drops next to them fully trackable, and `git add -A` will
# happily stage a real secrets file under any of those names.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

